      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2013-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Factoring \\(2^{2012}\\) from each term gives \\[ \\dfrac{2^{2012}(2^2 + 1)}{2^{2012}(2^2 - 1)} = \\dfrac{4 + 1}{4 - 1} = \\dfrac{5}{3}. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Factor \\(2^{2012}\\) out of both the numerator and the denominator",
        "The ratio reduces to \\(\\dfrac{2^2 + 1}{2^2 - 1}\\)"
      ],
